{{was wotd|2009|May|1}}
[[Image:Belgian barquentine Mercator. Trinidad, c. 1960.jpg|thumb|350px|The Belgian barquentine ''Mercator'' shown here has three masts: a square-rigged foremast on the left, a fore-and-aft-rigged mainmast in the middle, and a fore-and-aft-rigged '''mizzenmast''' on the right.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|mizenmast}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪz.ənˌmɑːst/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪz.ənˌmæst/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-mizzenmast.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[mizzen]][[mast]]}}

# {{label|en|nautical}} The [[aftmost]] [[mast]] on a ship having three or more masts
# {{label|en|nautical}} The second mast of a ship having two masts where the second one is shorter, such as a [[ketch]] or [[yawl]]

